**3. Memory note** (Write tool): `memory/ccs-wg-keepalive-relay.md`, plus one pointer line in `MEMORY.md`:

```markdown
---
name: ccs-wg-keepalive-relay
description: WG typing freezes / tunnel rebuilt every ~45 s = Pritunl keepalive PUT hitting the loopback-only console port; relay live on ccs-it 2026-09-28 (PR #165)
metadata:
  type: project
---
Pritunl WG clients send a keepalive PUT to <WG server address>:9700; the console listens on
loopback only, so every WG client rebuilt its tunnel. OpenVPN was never affected.
**Why:** the symptom looks like packet loss, but the cause is an unreachable HTTP keepalive.
**How to apply:** acceptance = operator's ping over WG (0% loss, 3 min, 2026-09-28);
rollback restores the failure, so move WG users to OpenVPN first. See [[project_ccs_v4_sites]].
```

